---
import { learningLibrary } from '../content/learning-library';
import { libraryEvidenceCounts } from '../content/first-project-policy.js';
const library = await learningLibrary();
const counts=libraryEvidenceCounts(library);
---
<div class="library-evidence" data-guides={counts.guides} data-fixtures={counts.fixtures} data-actual={counts.actual}>
 <p><strong>{counts.guides} reviewed guides</strong> · <strong>{counts.fixtures} executed fixture projects</strong> · <strong>{counts.actual} actual-data verified projects</strong>.</p>
 <details><summary>What this evidence establishes</summary>
  <p>{counts.approaches} documented approaches · {counts.practices} reviewed practices. Project runs are counted separately from guide completeness. A fixture run demonstrates the workflow; it establishes no competition score, historical reproduction or reader learning. Actual-data verification covers only its recorded scope.</p>
  <p><a href="/exercises/">Browse learning projects</a> · <a href="/milestones/">What these milestones mean</a></p>
 </details>
</div>
